Z||000000||speed racer||09-19-2000||05:12 PM||||Has any one ever raced a 92 stelth non-turbo if so what was the out come? I have a stock v-6.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||09-19-2000||05:25 PM||||Iv never raced a 92 no turbo. I have raced a 94 , It had factory twin turbos (I think) and the twin cam engine. Against my fairly stock V6. I kept up for about 4 seconds, and then he just floored it beat me by about 4 cars or so. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-19-2000||05:37 PM||||Back when I used to street race, I went against one with my Civic and smoked his tail. If he had been expecting my to launch hard, it would have been different but he just thought he could pull away easily and did not punch it hard at the start.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KitKar||09-19-2000||05:51 PM||||I have a 93 Stealth Non-Turbo. I will have to race them sometime. Right now my Fiero is not running so I can't. The Stealth has 118,000 miles, has tons of blue smoke come out the exhaust, and has a clogged catalytic converter. I think it would still beat my slightly modified 86 Fiero GT.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-19-2000||06:25 PM||||The twin turbo, hot rod version (remember Mitsubishi had the clone) will eat any stock Fiero for lunch.  Sorry, but that one's got around 300hp and an unGodly amount of torque for just a 3.?L V6.  Also, all wheel drive (wouldn't imagine much wheel spin), all wheel steering, etc, etc.  It probably weighs 1000# more, but I don't think you'd have much of a chance.  One of the slightly more generic versions can be beat easily.  (I have a friend with an '86GT/Getrag who raced one once.  Fiero-1  Stealth-less than 0)||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||09-19-2000||07:22 PM||||I raced a 3000GT(same as a Stealth) non-turbo with a 3.0 V6 and and automatic against my old '87 GT automatic(now 1FST2M6's) and could just barely pull away from him.  The GT was just a strong running 2.8 with a recent tune-up, ported heads, and ported manifolds w/ no cat. The 3000GT has something like 205hp without turbo's, but they weight just over 3500 lbs!!!  Now THAT is a fat car.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||DjKid||09-19-2000||07:39 PM||||just wanna poke a bit of info, the Stealth is a clone of the 3000GT, not the other way around.<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||09-19-2000||07:48 PM||||I raced my friends Stealth non-turbo and it was very close but I ended up a being a little bit faster. I have to mention I had my 65 series 205 snow tires on my car at the time though so I couldn't hook up off the launch!||||reg||1
Z||000008||whamel||09-19-2000||07:48 PM||||I was fooling around with an older base model Stealth in my GT a couple weeks ago.  We hit the light together and he couldn't stop laughing (okay, so my GT is ugly - it fits).  When the light turned green we took off, he beat me - but not by as much as he though he should have I'm sure.  At the next light, he took off nice and easy.<BR>One of my neighbors used to have a twin turbo that I used to race in my Daytona - now THAT's a fast car!  That and the Turbo 300zx that lived in my complex were about the best competition I could find in my piddly little town.<BR>FYI, My GT is pretty much stock (86 - 4spd) but it doesn't do too bad.  It needs a bit of work still though.<BR>Wade<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||KitKar||09-20-2000||01:02 PM||||The Stealth ES (No Turbo) has a 3.0L V6 and 222 HP. The Turbo model had 300 HP till about 94 then it was bumped to 320. There is also a base model with a single cam that has about 160 HP.<BR>I still think my P.O.S. Stealth would beat my 86 GT 5-speed. It would be close though.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||09-20-2000||09:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DjKid:<BR><B>just wanna poke a bit of info, the Stealth is a clone of the 3000GT, not the other way around.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ummm...technically, I got it right the 1st time.  Dodge and Mitsubishi are related (like Ford and Mazda).  The Dodge Stealth was introduced about 3 months before the Mitsubishi 3000GT.  That would make the Mitsu the clone although it doesn't really matter.  They're twins other than the fascias and wings.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||DjKid||09-20-2000||09:30 PM||||well, the Stealth is/was made by Mistubishi... you look under the hood of one, it will say mistubishi not Dodge... if you'd like I could post a pic tomorrow of under the hood of  a 93 ES... speedy lil demon!<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||stimpy||09-21-2000||01:57 AM||||Ahh, semantics... <BR>My understanding is that the Stealth and the 3000GT are both Diamond-Star Motors products, just like the Eagle Talon and it's siblings.  In other words, mechanicals by Mitsubishi, development $ by Chrysler.<BR>I do hope this clears up the fierce fighting and bloodshed regarding this matter.||||reg||1
Z||000013||BellaFiero||09-21-2000||10:27 AM||||"You see this scar? I got this in a Fierce and Bloody FLAME WAR!!!"<P>"oh my, that is an interesting scar... I do hope you've learned to stop picking your nose..."||||reg||1
Z||000014||Dan86gt3.8||09-22-2000||01:26 AM||||My dad as a 92 non turbo stealth and I drive it all the time.  It is no where close to my fiero.  If we were to race I would kill it.  But after all I'm not stock, but still I would say a manual 2.8 would beat a stealth no problem.<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000015||KitKar||09-22-2000||04:16 PM||||Dan86gt3.8, is your dads a 24 Valve or 16 Valve engine? There is a huge difference in performance.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000016||Dan86gt3.8||09-23-2000||03:24 PM||||I the 16 valve 3.0 liter.  I think it has 1 over head cam.  i think its a shitty car.  the auto tranny went out at like 50k.  It also burns oil.  he bought it used from some old people who had recprds ever sinse the car where they had the oil changed religously, but then again it has alott of neat electronic features and an airconditioning vent that aims striaght at your crotch!||||reg||1
Z||000017||StuGood||09-23-2000||03:33 PM||||I pulled up next to a black Stealth today, while driving my 1987 GT (stock V6 & 5-speed).  The GT managed to stay nose-to-nose with the Stealth for several minutes, then I watched as the Stealth's rear bumper filled  my view through the windshield.  Within a few seconds, the Stealth was at least 2 car lengths in front of the nose of my car.  I turned left, and went home. <P>I was backing out of my parking space at Sears, at the time (exchanging a twisted Torx socket for a new one)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> .    <P>       ||||reg||6
